{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-341022",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)g(-1)-f(-1){g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (2)}{(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
